{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"744dbbea33948d0239007a10862cdc071a9a6b79314f819f09ec04d8cd4639d8","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_3d6341b3ce41b5d98d6af5acab1bbf208cbe916fab1dafc26a2136fe4279b2c7","overall_assessment":"The paper presents two distinct contributions: theoretical regret bounds for EXP3.P in a Gaussian MAB setting with unbounded rewards, and an extension of EXP4 to RL (EXP4-RL) for exploration. The theoretical work offers a novel problem formulation and analysis, while the algorithmic work provides a creative combination of existing techniques with empirical validation on hard-to-explore games.","paper_id":"-5W5OBfFlwX","paper_identity_sha256":"3aa5c1bfe78b321b2f340cfebfdf11fbe009ff9771f71c87731c9be5d6aa3457","prompt_identity_sha256":"645c732f1c2c7bbd62259f71f56db8890d1f2b3fb60c41277bf12d2518b9269c","raw_response_sha256":"173581847608dc757edc10d24d1708dd84676554c104dae2ce7feba8021d97ac","request_identity_sha256":"de9ccc2815a26514cd12a46e306a65a31a62bff8e63ca97a56ca2591e8a75695","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"ORIG","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"47860fbf9ca9665e950e1db75e966827fe86a4ef0ebc69d508ec491f5aaed5f1","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-006","SRC-007","SRC-008"],"review_text":"The paper introduces a Gaussian Multi-Armed Bandit (MAB) setting where rewards follow a multivariate normal distribution and are unbounded. This formulation is presented as a novel problem that reflects the unbounded nature of rewards in Reinforcement Learning (RL), distinguishing it from classical adversarial or stochastic MAB settings which assume bounded rewards. The authors claim this setting addresses a gap in existing regret analyses that rely on boundedness assumptions.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-PROB"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-023","SRC-024","SRC-025"],"review_text":"The paper proposes EXP4-RL, an algorithm that extends the EXP4 framework from contextual bandits to RL. It utilizes deep Q-networks as experts with trust coefficients updated via exponential weighting. While the core mechanism is an adaptation of EXP4, the application to RL with DQN experts is presented as a new algorithmic approach to incentivize global exploration by combining multiple exploration strategies.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-MTH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-014","SRC-015","SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-019","SRC-020","SRC-021","SRC-022"],"review_text":"The paper provides novel theoretical insights by establishing both lower and upper bounds on regret for EXP3.P in the Gaussian MAB setting. It derives a linear lower bound for certain horizons and an upper bound of order O*(sqrt(T)) for large T, demonstrating that the standard O(sqrt(T)) regret order holds even without bounded rewards. The analysis includes a new construction of instances for the lower bound and adapts truncation techniques for the upper bound, offering a deeper understanding of EXP-type algorithms in unbounded reward scenarios.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-ANL"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-028","SRC-029","SRC-031","SRC-032","SRC-033","SRC-034","SRC-035"],"review_text":"The experimental setup evaluates the proposed EXP4-RL algorithm on two hard-to-explore RL games: Mountain Car and Montezuma's Revenge. The paper uses intrinsic reward as a metric for exploration performance, comparing against RND baselines. While the games are standard benchmarks, the specific focus on measuring global exploration via intrinsic reward spikes and AUC differences in the context of multi-expert RL provides a relevant evaluation protocol for the proposed method.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-EXP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-005","SRC-025","SRC-026","SRC-027"],"review_text":"The paper combines EXP4's expert weighting mechanism with deep Q-networks (specifically RND and epsilon-greedy DQN) to create a multi-expert exploration strategy. The rationale is that combining experts with different exploration behaviors (local vs. global) allows the algorithm to avoid getting stuck in local maxima, thereby achieving global exploration. This combination is presented as a creative synergy that leverages the strengths of individual RL exploration methods.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-COM"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not primarily focus on negative results or critical assessments of existing methods as a main contribution. While it identifies limitations of RND (local focus) and bounded reward assumptions in classical MAB, these are used to motivate the proposed positive contributions rather than serving as the central subject of a negative result analysis.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-NEG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"908a62d584718a9a1137aa12782926af8ff5588641d802cca896ebf3b1e1339f","paper_id":"-5W5OBfFlwX","paper_ordinal":106,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"173581847608dc757edc10d24d1708dd84676554c104dae2ce7feba8021d97ac","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"-5W5OBfFlwX","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"dc24ae325f0f36fd26ac377aa87d7b0766c0acfce2d4ec7e7117eb79b81fab07","request_identity_sha256":"de9ccc2815a26514cd12a46e306a65a31a62bff8e63ca97a56ca2591e8a75695","role":"ORIG","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":1074,"prompt_tokens":19274,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":20348},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"de9ccc2815a26514cd12a46e306a65a31a62bff8e63ca97a56ca2591e8a75695","role":"ORIG","role_ordinal":3,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}